WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.520
Instructor: When we rebase, we can end up with conflicts

00:02.520 --> 00:03.690
just like when we merge.

00:03.690 --> 00:04.980
We're combining history,

00:04.980 --> 00:06.870
we're combining branches together.

00:06.870 --> 00:08.910
That can lead to a merge conflict.

00:08.910 --> 00:11.040
So I'll just quickly demo that.

00:11.040 --> 00:12.840
We are on the feature branch.

00:12.840 --> 00:17.070
Let's change something on our website file.

00:17.070 --> 00:19.200
How about, I don't know,

00:19.200 --> 00:22.413
let's change this line that says footer added.

00:23.250 --> 00:27.000
Let's change it to say, what should we do?

00:27.000 --> 00:27.833
I don't know.

00:27.833 --> 00:29.040
How about, how about this?

00:29.040 --> 00:32.940
Instead of login form, we do log out form, added.

00:32.940 --> 00:35.160
I don't know why you need a form to log out, but sure.

00:35.160 --> 00:36.990
And then instead of navbar added,

00:36.990 --> 00:41.130
let's do top navbar added.

00:41.130 --> 00:43.590
Okay, not very exciting, but there we are.

00:43.590 --> 00:45.693
So I'm gonna add that and commit.

00:47.280 --> 00:48.113
And let's just go,

00:48.113 --> 00:52.050
let's say like update website on feature branch.

00:52.050 --> 00:53.550
I'm just putting on feat there,

00:53.550 --> 00:54.870
so you can see it in the message.

00:54.870 --> 00:57.030
You normally don't say what branch you're working on

00:57.030 --> 00:59.370
in a commit message, but I'm just doing that here

00:59.370 --> 01:00.660
so that we can see it.

01:00.660 --> 01:03.720
Now I'm gonna switch to master, right?

01:03.720 --> 01:07.566
And I'll do some more work on one of these lines.

01:07.566 --> 01:11.130
So instead of saying top navbar, I'll say,

01:11.130 --> 01:13.710
I don't know, main navbar.

01:13.710 --> 01:17.760
And instead of log out, I'll do, hmm,

01:17.760 --> 01:19.200
what should we say here?

01:19.200 --> 01:20.100
Sign up form?

01:20.100 --> 01:21.060
How about that?

01:21.060 --> 01:22.470
Sign up form added.

01:22.470 --> 01:25.050
So we should have some conflicts, right?

01:25.050 --> 01:27.150
And then we could even add something else.

01:27.150 --> 01:28.800
We'll let's start with that.

01:28.800 --> 01:31.863
Git commit dash am or on the master branch.

01:32.850 --> 01:36.003
Update copy on master.

01:37.440 --> 01:41.940
Okay, so now I'm gonna switch back to my feature branch.

01:41.940 --> 01:44.490
Let's do a tiny bit more work.

01:44.490 --> 01:49.490
Three, git commit dash am, right, more work on feat.

01:54.720 --> 01:56.790
All right, so here's what our history looks like

01:56.790 --> 01:58.110
in GitKraken.

01:58.110 --> 02:00.660
So we have a divergence,

02:00.660 --> 02:03.090
if that's the right way of saying that.

02:03.090 --> 02:05.370
We have our feature branch, which has some work.

02:05.370 --> 02:07.440
It's not a master, of course, quite a lot of work.

02:07.440 --> 02:09.420
But then, master has new work.

02:09.420 --> 02:11.490
We'll pretend we pulled that down.

02:11.490 --> 02:12.750
We didn't just type that ourself

02:12.750 --> 02:15.120
because that would be very stupid what I just showed you

02:15.120 --> 02:16.140
in the real world.

02:16.140 --> 02:18.510
But whatever that work is, it's coming from GitHub.

02:18.510 --> 02:19.343
We pull it down.

02:19.343 --> 02:21.960
It's a new feature our collaborators added in.

02:21.960 --> 02:23.370
I want that on feature.

02:23.370 --> 02:25.380
So I'm on the feature branch.

02:25.380 --> 02:27.420
I will rebase instead of merge.

02:27.420 --> 02:29.883
Git rebase and then master.

02:31.110 --> 02:33.750
And uh oh, look at this output.

02:33.750 --> 02:35.250
Slightly different, right?

02:35.250 --> 02:37.740
So it tries, it recreates all of our commits

02:37.740 --> 02:41.400
from the feature branch, rebasing them on the master branch.

02:41.400 --> 02:44.850
But then it gets to this, conflict,

02:44.850 --> 02:47.220
merge conflict in website.txt,

02:47.220 --> 02:49.140
failed to merge in changes.

02:49.140 --> 02:53.370
And if we look at our history, hmm, look at that.

02:53.370 --> 02:57.360
It is a partial rebase if you can see.

02:57.360 --> 02:58.500
I'll zoom in.

02:58.500 --> 03:02.730
So we have the feature branch, which is here,

03:02.730 --> 03:05.070
and it started to recreate our commit.

03:05.070 --> 03:08.340
So we have begin feature, we also have begin feature.

03:08.340 --> 03:10.440
We have work on feature, work on feature.

03:10.440 --> 03:13.560
We have more work on feature, more work on feature.

03:13.560 --> 03:15.810
So the rebase is not done.

03:15.810 --> 03:17.010
So I have a couple of choices.

03:17.010 --> 03:18.992
One, I can just abort the whole thing.

03:18.992 --> 03:20.910
It tells me exactly what to do.

03:20.910 --> 03:23.490
Here we are, to abort and get back to the state before,

03:23.490 --> 03:26.130
run git rebase, dash, dash abort.

03:26.130 --> 03:29.400
But basically, we are part of the way through rebasing.

03:29.400 --> 03:31.650
So it made new commits, some new commits,

03:31.650 --> 03:32.610
but it had a conflict.

03:32.610 --> 03:34.590
So we need to resolve that.

03:34.590 --> 03:35.850
So it tells us in this case,

03:35.850 --> 03:38.520
it's just one file, website.txt.

03:38.520 --> 03:41.610
I'll go in there, and I have to decide what to keep,

03:41.610 --> 03:43.740
what not to keep just like I would

03:43.740 --> 03:47.010
with any conflict or regular old merge conflict.

03:47.010 --> 03:48.582
So what should I do here?

03:48.582 --> 03:53.582
Let's say I want top navbar, but I want sign up form,

03:53.610 --> 03:56.910
so I can just, you know, manually do this.

03:56.910 --> 03:59.580
I'll do, get rid of that.

03:59.580 --> 04:01.920
I don't want main navbar.

04:01.920 --> 04:03.960
I want top navbar.

04:03.960 --> 04:05.850
So I can just manually reconfigure.

04:05.850 --> 04:08.010
I'm kind of just combining from two branches.

04:08.010 --> 04:10.380
I could have just gone with one or the other, of course,

04:10.380 --> 04:12.480
and often, that's what you do.

04:12.480 --> 04:15.750
But in this case, I'm gonna manually just combine them.

04:15.750 --> 04:18.420
So footer and then I want signup form.

04:18.420 --> 04:19.253
Okay.

04:20.220 --> 04:21.843
And then image gallery as well.

04:22.830 --> 04:25.350
All right, so that's kind of a messy way of resolving it.

04:25.350 --> 04:29.340
But that is the new version of this file that I want.

04:29.340 --> 04:30.450
Okay.

04:30.450 --> 04:33.750
So now it tells me, hopefully, you can see this.

04:33.750 --> 04:36.570
What I need to do is mark them as resolved by adding them.

04:36.570 --> 04:40.560
So git add the file, and then run git rebase,

04:40.560 --> 04:44.010
dash, dash continue, make this larger.

04:44.010 --> 04:46.620
Okay, so if I type git status,

04:46.620 --> 04:48.270
it tells me rebase in progress.

04:48.270 --> 04:49.820
Here's the commit that it's on.

04:50.700 --> 04:53.760
It tells me exactly where it is in this rebasing.

04:53.760 --> 04:56.640
So I'm going to add website

04:56.640 --> 04:58.893
because I fixed the conflict in there.

05:00.090 --> 05:02.460
Okay, but I'm not gonna commit.

05:02.460 --> 05:04.470
I'm going to run git rebase,

05:04.470 --> 05:06.600
dash, dash continue.

05:06.600 --> 05:08.460
So this is where you wanna just pay attention

05:08.460 --> 05:09.870
to the output, right?

05:09.870 --> 05:11.970
We just follow the instructions.

05:11.970 --> 05:13.440
It says all conflicts fixed.

05:13.440 --> 05:14.790
Now run this.

05:14.790 --> 05:18.810
Or I can abort the entire rebase using dash dash abort

05:18.810 --> 05:21.090
if I just wanna bail on it.

05:21.090 --> 05:25.020
Okay, so right now, rebase is paused,

05:25.020 --> 05:28.410
but I just continued it.

05:28.410 --> 05:29.243
Looks good.

05:29.243 --> 05:31.080
Let's type git status.

05:31.080 --> 05:33.660
All right, working to re-clean.

05:33.660 --> 05:35.760
And now we successfully completed the rebase,

05:35.760 --> 05:37.290
we resolved the conflicts,

05:37.290 --> 05:40.260
and the end result is that the changes from master

05:40.260 --> 05:42.330
and feature are all combined.

05:42.330 --> 05:43.163
They're integrated.

05:43.163 --> 05:46.050
So I have exactly what I wanted, right?

05:46.050 --> 05:48.870
I have this file resolved the way it is,

05:48.870 --> 05:50.430
and the entire feature branch,

05:50.430 --> 05:52.140
all that history was rewritten

05:52.140 --> 05:54.030
on top of the master branch,

05:54.030 --> 05:57.780
rebased on top of the tip of the master branch.

05:57.780 --> 05:58.613
All righty?

05:58.613 --> 05:59.700
So we still can have conflicts.

05:59.700 --> 06:01.620
We're still just combining commits

06:01.620 --> 06:03.210
or combining branches, rather.

06:03.210 --> 06:04.740
And that can lead to conflicts.

06:04.740 --> 06:06.450
The way you resolve them is the same.

06:06.450 --> 06:07.590
You go into the files.

06:07.590 --> 06:09.270
It tells you exactly where the conflict is.

06:09.270 --> 06:12.990
You pick what you want, incoming, original change,

06:12.990 --> 06:15.030
or a hybrid of them like we did.

06:15.030 --> 06:17.160
Then you add, you stage it,

06:17.160 --> 06:18.780
and then you follow the instructions.

06:18.780 --> 06:20.610
In our case, we don't wanna merge commit,

06:20.610 --> 06:22.230
so we don't do git commit.

06:22.230 --> 06:26.023
When we rebase, we did git rebase, dash, dash continue.

06:26.023 --> 06:27.123
All right.
